From 17023acf1af7c9b42c28bd54c1d7098b64617e78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 20:11:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(legal): separate the three models, gate statutory
 citations, fix break-even direction
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The site asserted "§42b EnWG" in ten places, including Schema.org FAQ markup
that search engines surface as a rich result. One answer read "Mieterstrom nach
§42b EnWG ist die direkte Lieferung ... im selben Gebäude oder Quartier, ohne
Nutzung des öffentlichen Netzes" — a statutory scope claim attached to the
wrong paragraph, indexed. Another dated a legislative simplification. Meanwhile
the brand talks Energy Sharing and the calculator models neither of those.

Rather than swap one unverified citation for another, this makes an unverified
citation structurally unable to reach a user.

- shared/legal-models.ts (new): the three models as distinct entries with their
  own scope, plus a citation record per model. formatCitation() returns null
  unless a human has verified the citation AND recorded a reference and a date.
  All three ship unverified, so the product now cites no paragraph anywhere —
  which is correct, because nobody has checked them. Counsel gets one file to
  review; verifying a model is a two-field change plus one boolean.
- legal-models.test.ts scans client/src, shared, server, api AND client/index.html
  and fails the build on any `§ n EnWG|EEG|BGB|MsbG` outside the register and
  the legal pages. "Never hard-code legal claims in UI copy" is now enforced,
  not aspirational. It caught all ten offenders on first run.
- index.html: paragraph citations removed from meta description, keywords, OG,
  Twitter, Organization description and knowsAbout. FAQ rewritten to describe
  the three models functionally without asserting statutory scope, plus a new
  entry that answers the question the product had been dodging: "Welches Modell
  rechnet der Rechner?" — Mieterstrom only, the other two are not computed, and
  no statement is made about legal admissibility. Dropped the undated
  Solarspitzengesetz simplification claim.
- The report and the calculator UI now carry a coverage statement generated
  from the register, so the claim cannot drift from it.
- Footer: "Allokation §42b EnWG" → "Allokationsrechner Energy Sharing".

Also fixes a wrong sentence customers act on. interpret.ts framed the
break-even threshold as an unmet hurdle regardless of position: a project
already at 13.6 % IRR was told "wirtschaftlich ab einer Investition von
~1506 €/kWp — aktuell 1210 €/kWp". The threshold is now direction-aware and
reads "Das Ziel von 10 % IRR ist bereits erreicht und bleibt erhalten, solange
die Investition unter ~1506 €/kWp liegt". New interpret.test.ts pins both
directions; the file previously had no tests at all.

PDF layout: the model row pushed the cashflow chart onto its own page and left
half of page 1 blank. Spacing tightened and a page-count regression test added.

Evidence: pnpm check clean, 75/75 vitest (18 new), pnpm build clean,
smoke-test 13/13.

